# Tertiary Structure Prediction

## Overview

Tertiary structure prediction involves determining the three-dimensional (3D) conformation of a protein from its amino acid sequence. 
The predicted structure provides insights into protein folding, stability, function, and molecular interactions. In this project, a
protein structure prediction server was used to generate the 3D model, which was subsequently refined and validated using appropriate 
bioinformatics tools.

## Objective

To predict the three-dimensional structure of the target protein for structural analysis and validation.

## Methodology

The protein sequence in FASTA format was submitted to a protein structure prediction server to generate a 3D model. The predicted
structure was then refined to improve its quality and validated using structure assessment tools.

## Input

* Protein sequence (FASTA).

## Output

* Predicted 3D protein model.
* Protein structure file (.pdb).
* Model confidence scores.

## Applications

* Structure-function analysis.
* Molecular docking studies.
* Drug discovery.
* Structural biology research.

## Files Included

* Protein sequence (FASTA).
* Predicted protein structure (.pdb).
* Structure prediction results.

## Conclusion

Tertiary structure prediction generated a three-dimensional model of the target protein, providing a structural basis for refinement, 
validation, and further computational analyses.

